cs, economics, statistics, and computing—including foundational work on Game/Theory, operator algebras, and the logical structure of modern digital computers; wartime work on the Manhattan Project and postwar defense and atomic-energy advisory roles.",["John von Neumann","About"]],["p-ecaf3f169a67bba1.html","source-block-595","Links",["John von Neumann"]],["p-ecaf3f169a67bba1.html","source-block-607","Wikipedia",["John von Neumann","Links"]],["p-dbf8e3b69a97542b.html","source-block-65","Johnny Gandelsman",[]],["p-dbf8e3b69a97542b.html","source-block-87","About",["Johnny Gandelsman"]],["p-dbf8e3b69a97542b.html","source-block-99","Violinist of Group/Brooklyn Rider and member of the Silk Road Ensemble.",["Johnny Gandelsman","About"]],["p-bd4927d1f6fb94fe.html","source-block-41","https://www.linkedin.com/in/hjohnny/",[]],["p-bd4927d1f6fb94fe.html","source-block-110","Co-Founder of",[]],["p-cb4f4630665ce750.html","source-block-41","Jonathan Blow",[]],["p-cb4f4630665ce750.html","source-block-59","About",["Jonathan Blow"]],["p-cb4f4630665ce750.html","source-block-71","Game designer and developer. On the On the Metal podcast, argued that composing many small Unix-style tools can yield inefficient systems without holistic architecture—drawing a parallel to microservices-style critiques of naïve modularity.",["Jonathan Blow","About"]],["p-cb4f4630665ce750.html","source-block-321","Online presence",["Jonathan Blow"]],["p-cb4f4630665ce750.html","source-block-343","Wikipedia",["Jonathan Blow","Online presence"]],["p-ae238dbe4f70a058.html","source-block-41","Jonathan Lear",[]],["p-ae238dbe4f70a058.html","source-block-59","About",["Jonathan Lear"]],["p-ae238dbe4f70a058.html","source-block-71","Author of Radical Hope: Ethics in the Face of Cultural Devastation.",["Jonathan Lear","About"]],["p-ae238dbe4f70a058.html","source-block-145","Source",["Jonathan Lear"]],["p-ae238dbe4f70a058.html","source-block-158","Reweaving Project spring 2027 syllabus",["Jonathan Lear","Source"]],["p-077d663dcd3bd05c.html","source-block-101","Radical Hope: Ethics in the Face of Cultural Devastation",[]],["p-077d663dcd3bd05c.html","source-block-203","About",["Radical Hope: Ethics in the Face of Cultural Devastation"]],["p-077d663dcd3bd05c.html","source-block-215","Examines hope and ethical life when a culture’s familiar concepts and practices collapse, through the experience of Crow leader Plenty Coups.",["Radical Hope: Ethics in the Face of Cultural Devastation","About"]],["p-077d663dcd3bd05c.html","source-block-363","Original publisher: Harvard University Press.",["Radical Hope: Ethics in the Face of Cultural Devastation","About"]],["p-077d663dcd3bd05c.html","source-block-413","Links",["Radical Hope: Ethics in the Face of Cultural Devastation"]],["p-077d663dcd3bd05c.html","source-block-425","Course/Reweaving Project/Syllabus/2027 Spring",["Radical Hope: Ethics in the Face of Cultural Devastation","Links"]],["p-077d663dcd3bd05c.html","source-block-479","Author’s university on the book",["Radical Hope: Ethics in the Face of Cultural Devastation","Links"]],["p-4f8490f9afb1f0ec.html","source-block-41","Jonathan Rowson",[]],["p-4f8490f9afb1f0ec.html","source-block-61","About",["Jonathan Rowson"]],["p-4f8490f9afb1f0ec.html","source-block-73","Author of “Prefixing the World,” “Deactivating the H2 Vortex,” and “Bildung in the 21st Century.”",["Jonathan Rowson","About"]],["p-4f8490f9afb1f0ec.html","source-block-187","Source",["Jonathan Rowson"]],["p-4f8490f9afb1f0ec.html","source-block-200","Reweaving Project spring 2027 syllabus",["Jonathan Rowson","Source"]],["p-0446c2cdfd8ca9a2.html","source-block-0","Sound (German: Klang)",[]],["p-2b78a3d51a7d3f8a.html","source-block-41","Jordan Lord",[]],["p-2b78a3d51a7d3f8a.html","source-block-57","About",["Jordan Lord"]],["p-2b78a3d51a7d3f8a.html","source-block-69","Builds radically simple, open tools and worlds through constraint-driven engineering (from jordanlord.co.uk).",["Jordan Lord","About"]],["p-2b78a3d51a7d3f8a.html","source-block-220","Online presence",["Jordan Lord"]],["p-2b78a3d51a7d3f8a.html","source-block-242","Site · Blog index · Projects · Contact",["Jordan Lord","Online presence"]],["p-2b78a3d51a7d3f8a.html","source-block-423","GitHub (logiclogue) · YouTube · LinkedIn · Twitter / X",["Jordan Lord","Online presence"]],["p-2b78a3d51a7d3f8a.html","source-block-667","Writing",["Jordan Lord"]],["p-2b78a3d51a7d3f8a.html","source-block-681","Person/Jordan Lord/Blog/26/04/07/3 constraints before I build anything",["Jordan Lord","Writing"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-30","3 constraints before I build anything",[]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-120","Author: Person/Jordan Lord",["3 constraints before I build anything"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-158","Published: 2026-04-07 (on jordanlord.co.uk)",["3 constraints before I build anything"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-253","Summary",["3 constraints before I build anything"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-267","Person/Jordan Lord argues constraints enable creativity: they shrink the search space so you can find sharper solutions. After ~10 years building, he uses three gates before starting anything; if an idea fails any of them, he does not build it.",["3 constraints before I build anything","Summary"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-532","The three constraints",["3 constraints before I build anything"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-560","1. One page or it doesn’t get built — Write a single one-pager per idea: north star, non‑negotiable, precise, ambitious, lean. Use it for investors, collaborators, and yourself. If something matters in a dispute, it belongs in the one-pager or the one-pager changes; otherwise it is not the fight. If you cannot fill one page without fluff, you are not ready—research, plan, prototype, rewrite. If it needs more than one page, it is too complex to build (yet).",["3 constraints before I build anything","The three constraints"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-1049","2. The core tech must be separable from the product — Ship a core capability (method, skill, tool, or extractable library) that supports the product but survives without it—reusable IP that compounds while products pivot. Examples in the post: git for Linux, HCL for HashiCorp, Kubernetes at Google; yours might be smaller (a library or a methodology). If the idea does not enable core tech, it is not high enough leverage.",["3 constraints before I build anything","The three constraints"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-1517","3. One defining constraint must shape the product — Pick one obvious constraint users see constantly; it is the product’s identity and limits feature creep (e.g. Minecraft’s blocks, IKEA’s flat-pack). A good constraint reduces decision space so design can “fall out” of it; weak or missing constraints yield bloated “do everything” products. That constraint should also be front and centre in the one-pager.",["3 constraints before I build anything","The three constraints"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-1977","Closing rule (from post)",["3 constraints before I build anything"]],["p-8fc992043c59fdcf.html","source-block-2008","If it fails any of the three, do not build it.",["3 constraints before I build anything","Closing rule (from post)"]],["p-06d3bc9fca5220f3.html","source-block-114","Josean Martinez",[]],["p-06d3bc9fca5220f3.html","source-block-134","About",["Josean Martinez"]],["p-06d3bc9fca5220f3.html","source-block-146","YouTube creator focused on Neovim, Lazygit, and terminal workflows",["Josean Martinez","About"]],["p-06d3bc9fca5220f3.html","source-block-225","Shares dotfiles, setup guides, and how to integrate tools like Lazygit with Neovim and lazy.nvim",["Josean Martinez","About"]],["p-06d3bc9fca5220f3.html","source-block-326","Web",["Josean Martinez"]],["p-06d3bc9fca5220f3.html","source-block-336","Newsletter: https://buttondown.email/josean",["Josean Martinez","Web"