lone desktop app.",["phosphor"]],["p-8d7cfe51e96a7838.html","source-block-284","Written in Rust by a non-rust dev. 70 commits in a few days, not updated since.",["phosphor"]],["p-8d7cfe51e96a7838.html","source-block-371","GitHub/Star count: 5 (checked 2026-07-12).",["phosphor"]],["p-8d7cfe51e96a7838.html","source-block-421","Includes built-in synths, undo history, Vim-style keybindings, and recording driven from the terminal.",["phosphor"]],["p-8d7cfe51e96a7838.html","source-block-527","could be useful reference for a more personalized project.",["phosphor"]],["p-d5e36968bbef2cc5.html","source-block-43","jlevy/flowmark: Better auto-formatting for Markdown",[]],["p-d5e36968bbef2cc5.html","source-block-136","See - Reddit/Python/25/07/flowmark - a better auto-formatter for Markdown",["jlevy/flowmark: Better auto-formatting for Markdown"]],["p-6cf5549e39a26757.html","source-block-0","Unmasking AI: My Mission to Protect What Is Human in a World of Machines",[]],["p-14daff5cc4d386b1.html","source-block-72","Juan Bindez",[]],["p-14daff5cc4d386b1.html","source-block-88","About",["Juan Bindez"]],["p-14daff5cc4d386b1.html","source-block-100","Creator and maintainer of pytubefix; based in Brazil.",["Juan Bindez","About"]],["p-14daff5cc4d386b1.html","source-block-162","Online presence",["Juan Bindez"]],["p-14daff5cc4d386b1.html","source-block-184","https://github.com/JuanBindez",["Juan Bindez","Online presence"]],["p-14daff5cc4d386b1.html","source-block-218","Profile of Juan_Bindez · PyPI",["Juan Bindez","Online presence"]],["p-14daff5cc4d386b1.html","source-block-291","Projects",["Juan Bindez"]],["p-14daff5cc4d386b1.html","source-block-306","pytubefix — Python3 library for downloading YouTube videos (JuanBindez/pytubefix).",["Juan Bindez","Projects"]],["p-95f478476af748a6.html","source-block-117","Judah ha-Nasi",[]],["p-95f478476af748a6.html","source-block-182","About",["Judah ha-Nasi"]],["p-95f478476af748a6.html","source-block-194","Rabbi Judah the Prince (about 135 to 217 CE), head of the Sanhedrin in Roman Galilee, under whom the Judaism/Mishnah was compiled around 200 CE.",["Judah ha-Nasi","About"]],["p-9c9ab3d051afaf80.html","source-block-213","Julie Battilana",[]],["p-9c9ab3d051afaf80.html","source-block-287","About",["Julie Battilana"]],["p-9c9ab3d051afaf80.html","source-block-299","Coauthor of Power, for All with Tiziana Casciaro.",["Julie Battilana","About"]],["p-9c9ab3d051afaf80.html","source-block-355","Academic Appointment",["Julie Battilana"]],["p-9c9ab3d051afaf80.html","source-block-382","Joseph C. Wilson Professor of Business Administration at Harvard Business School and Alan L. Gleitsman Professor of Social Innovation at Harvard Kennedy School. Her research concerns power and social change.",["Julie Battilana","Academic Appointment"]],["p-9c9ab3d051afaf80.html","source-block-594","Source",["Julie Battilana"]],["p-9c9ab3d051afaf80.html","source-block-607","Reweaving Project spring 2027 syllabus",["Julie Battilana","Source"]],["p-89085bf92fb4d965.html","source-block-41","Juliette van der Laarse",[]],["p-89085bf92fb4d965.html","source-block-69","Role: Engineering Manager (international financial services firm)",["Juliette van der Laarse"]],["p-89085bf92fb4d965.html","source-block-142","Bio: Juliette van der Laarse presents the AI Flower, a public capability architecture for orienting engineers and teams from scattered AI experiments to integrated, accountable practice—using a “skill fossilization” lens as tools churn.",["Juliette van der Laarse"]],["p-89085bf92fb4d965.html","source-block-396","Related Events:",["Juliette van der Laarse"]],["p-89085bf92fb4d965.html","source-block-419","OReilly/Event/26/03/AI Codecon",["Juliette van der Laarse","Related Events:"]],["p-89085bf92fb4d965.html","source-block-458","OReilly/Event/26/03/AI Codecon/1410 AI Flower Juliette van der Laarse",["Juliette van der Laarse","Related Events:"]],["p-10c5dc0a6f246dc0.html","source-block-41","https://www.linkedin.com/in/qedpi/",[]],["p-7fa15b9ffb4813c0.html","source-block-73","Justin M. Keyes",[]],["p-7fa15b9ffb4813c0.html","source-block-124","Long-time Neovim maintainer and project lead (GitHub justinmk); central to releases, roadmap, and core editor architecture from the early fork era onward.",["Justin M. Keyes"]],["p-7fa15b9ffb4813c0.html","source-block-290","Links",["Justin M. Keyes"]],["p-7fa15b9ffb4813c0.html","source-block-302","GitHub: justinmk",["Justin M. Keyes","Links"]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-58","https://github.com/karenetheridge",[]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-128","https://stackoverflow.com/users/40468/ether",[]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-215","https://www.linkedin.com/in/karenetheridge/",[]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-517","Member of the Perl Core Team: https://perldoc.perl.org/perlgov#The-Core-Team",["https://www.linkedin.com/in/karenetheridge/"]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-601","I write code, much of it in Perl, for a variety of real-world applications, most recently for building and maintaining network infrastructure. I work on the full stack, from front end UIs down to hardware interfaces, in technologies such as Mojolicious, PostgreSQL, Nginx, Ansible and Docker to keep critical systems running and make them faster, more reliable and provide features that fulfill business objectives and thrill users.",["https://www.linkedin.com/in/karenetheridge/","Member of the Perl Core Team: https://perldoc.perl.org/perlgov#The-Core-Team"]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-1038","In my spare time I volunteer in a variety of ways to make the Perl language and infrastructure better, participating in working groups and committees and authoring and maintaining open source software on CPAN and Github.",["https://www.linkedin.com/in/karenetheridge/","Member of the Perl Core Team: https://perldoc.perl.org/perlgov#The-Core-Team"]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-1306","I have worked remotely for ten years quite successfully, and at this point in time am not considering in-office employment.",["https://www.linkedin.com/in/karenetheridge/"]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-1433","It is okay to tell me about new job opportunities. It is NOT okay to try to sell me your company's products or services. I do not make purchasing decisions.",["https://www.linkedin.com/in/karenetheridge/"]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-1593","Job pitches are much more likely to elicit a response if you tell me up front about the tech stack you are using and the product space you're in.",["https://www.linkedin.com/in/karenetheridge/"]],["p-dc19dfcb0e334f1f.html","source-block-1742","Member of the JSON Schema Organization's Technical Steering Committee: json-schema.org",["https://www.linkedin.com/in/karenetheridge/"]],["p-b8de0fbf07081ae3.html","source-block-42","Kasper Zutterman",[]],["p-b8de0fbf07081ae3.html","source-block-95","About",["Kasper Zutterman"]],["p-b8de0fbf07081ae3.html","source-block-107","Senior data engineer in Belgium; maintains Person/Kasper Zutterman/GitHub/Second-Brain, a curated index of public digital gardens.",["Kasper Zutterman","About"]],["p-b8de0fbf07081ae3.html","source-block-246","Projects",["Kasper Zutterman"]],["p-b8de0fbf07081ae3.html","source-block-261","Person/Kasper Zutterman/GitHub/Second-Brain",["Kasper Zutterman","Projects"]],["p-b8de0fbf07081ae3.html","source-block-313","Links",["Kasper Zutterman"]],["p-b8de0fbf07081ae3.html","source-block-325","Website",["Kasper Zutterman","Links"]],["p-b8de0fbf07081ae3.html","source-block-369","GitHub",["Kasper Zutterman","Links"]],["p-c57f4edb45fba415.html","source-block-123","Second-Brain",[]],["p-c57f4edb45fba415.html","source-block-191","GitHub/Star count: 1842 (checked 2026-09-20 Sun)",["Second-Brain"]],["p-c57f4edb45fba415.html","source-block-251","Curated list of public Zettelkastens, second brains, and digital gardens, maintained by Person/Kasper Zutterman.",["Second-Brain"]],["p-c57f4edb45fba415.html","so